This is the rank-one finiteness argument the maintainer asks for, following Gross's exposition of Kolyvagin: if y_K has infinite order then E(K) has rank one and Ш(E/K) is finite. HE.3–HE.7 plan it. The missing items are the argument's steps that those stages do not state:
- local Kummer theory at the Kolyvagin primes: the unramified image, the isotropy (7.1)–(7.4), and the dimension of H¹(K_λ,E)_p;
- Kolyvagin's formula for the local pairing (7.6), and the ±-eigenspace dimensions (Proposition 8.1);
- the whole Čebotarev and Kummer-duality argument of §9 over L = K(E_p): the pairing (9.2), L_S, Proposition 9.3, the structure of H⁺ and I⁺ (Proposition 9.5), and Proposition 9.6;
- the facts that Mazur's theorem supplies the GL₂ image and that Proposition 2.1 applies to almost all p;
- the classes d(n) in Ш(E/K)_p when p | y_K (§11), and the Bertolini–Darmon remark (§12).
Gross proves the clean case (Propositions 2.1/2.3). Kolyvagin's full bound #Ш | t·I_K² (Theorem 1.3) is only quoted there, so HE.7's all-prime statement still needs Kolyvagin's article or another source. Review (REV-PAPER-KOLYVAGIN-90): HE.6 plans the Kolyvagin bound only under Howard's hypotheses (p ∤ DN and surjectivity onto GL₂(ℤ_p)); Gross needs only mod-p surjectivity and allows p | N, so Proposition 2.1 (Ш), Proposition 2.3 and Claims 10.1 and 10.3 join this route as missing, together with the unramified cohomology of E and the component group (Milne), which belongs with HE.3's local conditions. The local pairing formula (7.6) and the dimension of H¹(K_λ,E)_p are Rubin's Lemma I.4.7 and the local duality of SelmerIwasawaCohomology L1, both planned (ES.1, L1), and leave the route. The isotropy (7.4), the reduction of eigenspaces (3.4), the absence of p-torsion over K and the §9 set-up are planned in HE.4–HE.6 and stay in the route as planned items Gross is a good source for.
